WEBVTT

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:20.790
You there! Stop! Take off your hood!

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:22.460
Who? Me?

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:24.500
D-Did you do something wrong?

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:25.960
O-Of course not!

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:27.630
Remove your hood!

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:33.220
H-Hey. Come on.

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:35.350
It's not him.

00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:39.940
Lieutenant Yuito Sumeragi is accused
of sabotaging a government facility.

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:43.400
Authorities are on high alert
as they try to find him.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:45.820
In other news...

00:01:05.130 --> 00:01:06.420
<i>A crime in reality</i>

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:07.710
<i>For Heaven's sake</i>

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:09.630
<i>Accepts any fake</i>

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:12.050
<i>And disappears</i>

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:15.140
<i>Piling the eternity in fantasy</i>

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:16.680
<i>Won't take it at all</i>

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:17.760
<i>I get sick</i>

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:19.680
<i>A girl looking back</i>

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:22.100
<i>Casts the miracle</i>

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:25.060
<i>Into the instant world </i>

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:29.940
<i>Did you lie?</i>

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:31.780
<i>Did you lie?</i>

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:34.860
<i>Spit the venom </i>

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:39.620
<i>I know why</i>

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:43.210
<i>I've found a game of ecstasy</i>

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:45.830
<i>Red Criminal gets life</i>

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:48.300
<i>I've never been in love</i>

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:54.130
<i>Don't know when I started</i>
<i>getting sick of this world</i>

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:55.720
<i>We will fly</i>

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:58.560
<i>Someday I won't be crying</i>

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:03.390
<i>I've been sacrificing myself</i>

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:05.810
<i>Not to hurt anybody</i>

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:23.240
TOGETSU

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:19.660
That really sucks.

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:23.750
First, they build you up to be a hero,
and now they call you a rebel.

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:28.670
Well, that whole hero thing
never made much sense.

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:32.090
Anyway, I'm just glad you're here, Wataru.

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:37.720
When they branded me a rebel, I was
worried it would endanger you, too.

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:40.850
I had a meeting with Major General Fubuki.

00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:45.230
I said if anything happened to you guys,
I'd flee to the hideout.

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:49.690
Have you heard from
Major General Fubuki since then?

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:55.150
The last I heard from him was when
you left the Old OSF Hospital.

00:02:55.150 --> 00:03:00.160
But from that point, he vanished
from every single system.

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:03.580
I hope he hasn't fallen
into government hands.

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:09.290
If Major General Fubuki hadn't shown up...

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:12.710
In an effort to establish
countermeasures for future duds,

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:18.260
we should dissect the subject
and collect his brain data.

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:19.680
Something wrong?

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:23.350
No, I'm just thinking about
what happened at the hospital.

00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:28.270
That's right. You were held in a
separate room from the rest of us.

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:34.150
The doctor said that I had been a dud.

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:35.740
I don't understand.

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:38.530
You can use psionics, can't you?

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:40.910
I don't really understand myself.

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:45.080
Maybe it's some sort of misunderstanding.

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:46.870
Yeah, but that is concerning.

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:48.330
Yeah.

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:52.090
But right now, I'd like to
discuss what comes next.

00:03:52.090 --> 00:03:54.670
Are you sure, Yuito?

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:59.380
Yeah, we need to plan our next move.

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:01.640
We can't stay in Suoh.

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:06.930
But the situation in Seiran
isn't much different.

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:10.600
So I was thinking,
why not head for Togetsu?

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:14.820
It's preserved its independence
as a theocratic autonomous zone.

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:18.530
And they'll have info
we can't get in Suoh or Seiran.

00:04:18.530 --> 00:04:20.360
Togetsu.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:24.780
Come to think of it,
Karen mentioned Togetsu, too.

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:27.500
But we don't know
my brother's true intent.

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:29.210
About that...

00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:37.010
A while back, I heard from my uncle
that he had business dealings in Togetsu.

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:41.380
You mean your uncle and the OSF Hospital?

00:04:42.390 --> 00:04:44.180
What sort of business?

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:46.180
I don't know the details.

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:50.640
If it involves the OSF Hospital,
it probably has something to do

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:54.190
with psionics research
and metamorphosis tech.

00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:59.570
He was also involved with Seiran,
so is going to Togetsu a good idea?

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:01.820
Yeah, I can't be sure.

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:07.160
But if the hospital is involved,
going to Togetsu makes sense.

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:11.290
Unlike my father and brother,

00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:15.880
I grew up clueless about
the truth behind this country.

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:19.880
There's still probably a lot
of things I don't know.

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:22.130
So I want to know everything.

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:27.640
If there's a way to get even a little bit
of new information, I have to try.

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:37.190
If that's what our commander wants,
count me in.

00:05:37.190 --> 00:05:39.650
So then it's decided.

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:47.910
We're going to Togetsu!

00:05:52.710 --> 00:05:55.080
Instead of sitting around in frustration,

00:05:55.080 --> 00:06:00.050
you should try to find
a way to save Naomi.

00:06:03.260 --> 00:06:04.970
I heard the news.

00:06:04.970 --> 00:06:08.220
You're going to Togetsu? Seriously?

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:10.390
I haven't decided yet.

00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:11.600
But...

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:18.820
I had Haruka look into the truck routes
to and from the facility where Naomi is.

00:06:18.820 --> 00:06:22.690
It seems they're traveling
between Togetsu and the facility.

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:26.160
They were unregistered.

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:30.240
But based on their route,
they're definitely going to Togetsu.

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:34.460
So the human brains used to make
the drug in those ampules

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:38.290
are most likely being supplied by Togetsu.

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:42.050
Whoa, whoa, think about
what you're saying, Kyoka.

00:06:42.050 --> 00:06:44.970
Togetsu's not some sort
of horrible bogeyman!

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:46.010
Oh, right.

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:50.760
You've mentioned you're from Togetsu
and a missionary for the Togetsu faith.

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:54.680
Togetsu's home to a faith that
worships the Moon, and that's it.

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:57.400
I never heard about Others and whatnot.

00:06:57.400 --> 00:07:00.360
However, Togetsu's history goes way back.

00:07:00.360 --> 00:07:05.400
I wouldn't be surprised if they possessed
information we know nothing about.

00:07:07.700 --> 00:07:12.910
We now know about the research facility
and that Karen can help my sister.

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:19.710
But the more I think about it,
there is far too much we don't know.

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:23.420
Yeah, we're talking about
experimentation using human brains.

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:26.630
Who knows what the hell Karen is thinking.

00:07:26.630 --> 00:07:30.720
I have a feeling he's still
withholding information,

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:33.560
including about Suoh and Seiran, too.

00:07:33.560 --> 00:07:39.730
It's not in our best interest to waste any
more time putting our trust in Karen.

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:45.030
In Togetsu, we just might learn
something that will save Naomi.

00:07:45.030 --> 00:07:47.820
Kasane, what do <i>you </i>want to do?

00:07:48.910 --> 00:07:50.990
I want to go to Togetsu

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:53.790
if there's even a small chance
it might save Naomi.

00:07:53.790 --> 00:07:56.330
Wait! Seriously, Kasane?!

00:07:56.330 --> 00:07:58.500
Remember what Karen said?

00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:03.500
"Who knows what Seiran will do to
Naomi if we make a wrong move?"

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:08.630
Kagero, it's as if you don't
want us to go to Togetsu.

00:08:08.630 --> 00:08:12.760
Is going there that big of a problem?

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:16.640
I'm sure Naomi will be fine here.

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:21.310
Karen wants to protect
the research facility.

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:25.440
He won't allow Seiran
to interfere in their work.

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:28.490
How can you be so sure?

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:34.950
We go way back,
so I know at least that much.

00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:37.250
How about you, Haruka?

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:42.750
I'll monitor the research facility
and Seiran's moves.

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:46.000
I'll contact you immediately
if anything happens.

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:48.470
Thank you. I'm in your debt.

00:08:48.470 --> 00:08:50.340
So it's decided.

00:08:55.970 --> 00:08:57.600
Good grief.

00:09:08.240 --> 00:09:11.910
Sis? Sis?

00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:32.090
Sis?

00:09:39.980 --> 00:09:44.150
I promise. I <i>will </i>save you!

00:10:25.270 --> 00:10:27.610
You're awake.

00:10:27.610 --> 00:10:29.610
Thanks to you.

00:10:29.610 --> 00:10:33.740
Here you are again, coming to my rescue.

00:10:33.740 --> 00:10:36.820
I can't afford to lose you.

00:10:37.820 --> 00:10:43.000
Is that because I'm engaged to Alice?

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:49.090
You're still a regiment commander
in the Suoh OSF. That hasn't changed.

00:10:49.090 --> 00:10:51.840
That means you're still useful.

00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:53.720
I see.

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:57.840
Do you remember?

00:10:57.840 --> 00:11:03.480
The day Alice joined the force,
it was sunny, just like today.

00:11:09.230 --> 00:11:11.860
She was so happy.

00:11:11.860 --> 00:11:15.200
She had finally caught up with us.

00:11:18.910 --> 00:11:22.580
But truth be told, I was worried.

00:11:22.580 --> 00:11:26.250
She is too gentle a soul.

00:11:26.250 --> 00:11:30.170
She wasn't cut out to be a soldier.

00:11:30.170 --> 00:11:33.840
Plus, she's clumsy and scatterbrained.

00:11:35.010 --> 00:11:40.720
Alice was always getting mad at you
for saying things like that.

00:11:40.720 --> 00:11:44.520
But she didn't really mean it.

00:11:44.520 --> 00:11:49.060
I never imagined I'd lose Alice like that.

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:02.740
Have you ever thought about it?

00:12:02.740 --> 00:12:06.250
If she'd left the service
without incident,

00:12:06.250 --> 00:12:09.040
what would things be like now?

00:12:13.840 --> 00:12:17.220
There's no point thinking about that.

00:12:34.020 --> 00:12:36.860
What will become of me?

00:12:36.860 --> 00:12:39.740
I can't take it anymore. I'm scared.

00:12:39.740 --> 00:12:41.570
It's unbearable.

00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:46.080
Someone... Someone help me.

00:12:46.080 --> 00:12:47.700
Don't...

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:51.120
I'll... friend.

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:54.170
Don't cry.

00:12:54.170 --> 00:12:56.300
It's all right.

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:08.310
Haruka, we've veered far
from our patrol route.

00:13:08.310 --> 00:13:10.640
How do things look over there?

00:13:10.640 --> 00:13:13.230
No one's noticed yet,
as far as I can tell.

00:13:13.230 --> 00:13:15.940
I'll monitor the situation as best I can.

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:18.650
Thank you. I feel better knowing that.

00:13:25.580 --> 00:13:28.200
This is as far as we can go by truck.

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:30.250
I-I-I'm f-f-freezing...

00:13:30.250 --> 00:13:33.750
I heard it was cold here,
but not this bad.

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:36.420
Right? It's freezing, isn't it?

00:13:36.420 --> 00:13:39.300
Some areas get snow year-round.

00:13:39.300 --> 00:13:40.800
It sucks, doesn't it?

00:13:40.800 --> 00:13:43.430
S-S-So... c-c-cold...

00:13:43.430 --> 00:13:48.220
If we don't keep moving,
it will feel even colder.

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:52.890
Yeah, she's right.

00:13:52.890 --> 00:13:59.190
The weather sucks, and we could get
stranded if it turns into a blizzard.

00:13:59.190 --> 00:14:03.700
It's still not too late to head back
and gather around a steamy hot pot.

00:14:03.700 --> 00:14:06.370
S-S-So c-c-cold.

00:14:06.370 --> 00:14:08.080
Shut it, Kagero.

00:14:08.080 --> 00:14:12.540
You know you want to head back
and warm your bones in a toasty bed.

00:14:12.540 --> 00:14:16.590
Let's be honest with ourselves, Shiden.

00:14:16.590 --> 00:14:18.880
I-I'm f-freezing.

00:14:16.590 --> 00:14:18.880
Enough already, Arashi!

00:14:18.880 --> 00:14:21.550
Will you three stop screwing around!

00:14:21.550 --> 00:14:25.010
Wha--?! Don't lump me in
with those morons!

00:14:38.190 --> 00:14:41.110
I can't believe flowers can bloom up here.

00:14:41.110 --> 00:14:42.940
Yeah.

00:14:42.940 --> 00:14:46.530
I bet Tsugumi would love to see them.

00:14:46.530 --> 00:14:51.450
There are stranger things
than flowers here.

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:55.040
Snowfields teaming with Others
aren't uncommon.

00:14:55.040 --> 00:14:59.040
But no one knows where they come from.

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:02.710
The mystery of
the never-melting snowfields.

00:15:02.710 --> 00:15:08.470
No wonder it's a mystery. I mean,
who can think when their brain is frozen?

00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:12.810
We've been walking for some time now.
Are we any closer to Togetsu?

00:15:12.810 --> 00:15:15.310
Yeah, we should be there soon.

00:15:16.480 --> 00:15:20.570
It's kind of late to ask,
but what's the city like?

00:15:20.570 --> 00:15:23.110
Strictly speaking, it's not a city.

00:15:23.110 --> 00:15:26.700
It's really just a facility
for the Togetsu faith.

00:15:26.700 --> 00:15:29.740
Just a bunch of weirdos
obsessed with the Moon.

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:32.450
It was a truly stifling environment.

00:15:33.450 --> 00:15:37.370
It's not nice to call them weirdos.

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:40.090
Ever hear of freedom of religion?

00:15:40.090 --> 00:15:42.460
Depends on the beliefs in question.

00:15:42.460 --> 00:15:43.800
Exactly.

00:15:43.800 --> 00:15:47.630
Kagero, you may not have fond memories,

00:15:47.630 --> 00:15:51.050
but we must try to understand one another.

00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:53.600
Understand each other? Right...

00:15:55.770 --> 00:15:58.350
The weather took a turn for the worst.

00:15:58.350 --> 00:16:01.650
Haruka, how does the weather
in this area look?

00:16:01.650 --> 00:16:03.360
That's strange.

00:16:03.360 --> 00:16:06.190
All my data points to it being sunny.

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:08.030
How's that possible?

00:16:09.410 --> 00:16:12.660
Huh? There's something ahead.

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:20.080
What is <i>that</i>?!

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:26.340
Kyoka!

00:16:26.340 --> 00:16:27.720
An Other made of ice?!

00:16:27.720 --> 00:16:29.840
That's something new.

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:56.160
Sheesh. Others sure do come in
all shapes and sizes.

00:16:56.160 --> 00:16:58.580
But one made of ice?

00:17:00.080 --> 00:17:02.080
The blizzard's over.

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:04.920
That Other was behind it.

00:17:06.710 --> 00:17:10.130
What in the world are Others, anyway?

00:17:10.130 --> 00:17:14.430
Who knows? The ruined mess
of evolution gone wrong?

00:17:14.430 --> 00:17:21.270
Even the OSF knows nothing more than they
rain down from the Extinction Belt.

00:17:21.270 --> 00:17:23.230
That's true.

00:17:25.440 --> 00:17:26.780
Look.

00:17:36.910 --> 00:17:38.790
It's strangely quiet.

00:17:38.790 --> 00:17:42.540
Yeah, no sign of anyone around.

00:17:44.170 --> 00:17:49.380
Well, sorry, but this is as far as I go.

00:17:51.840 --> 00:17:56.470
A reunion with my fellow countrymen
doesn't sound all that fun.

00:17:56.470 --> 00:17:58.890
All right, catch you later.

00:17:58.890 --> 00:18:00.480
Hey, wait!

00:18:01.430 --> 00:18:03.770
What's with him?

00:18:05.400 --> 00:18:09.280
Sister Kasane, we welcome you home.

00:18:09.280 --> 00:18:12.570
Sister Kasane, you are our treasure.

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:15.120
We have awaited you.

00:18:16.830 --> 00:18:18.700
You know who I am?

00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:21.200
What do you mean by "treasure"?

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:24.580
Kasane, does any of this ring a bell?

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:26.540
No, I'm drawing a blank.

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:30.420
I have no connection
with the Togetsu faith.

00:18:30.420 --> 00:18:34.090
It is no wonder you do not remember.

00:18:34.090 --> 00:18:38.810
However, Sister Kasane,
you are originally from Togetsu.

00:18:38.810 --> 00:18:40.220
I am?

00:18:40.220 --> 00:18:46.440
Yes. You were born
with immense psionic power.

00:18:46.440 --> 00:18:53.110
The New Himukan government kidnapped you
after expressing interest in your power.

00:18:55.240 --> 00:18:57.280
That's not true.

00:18:57.280 --> 00:19:01.700
My parents were killed by Others
when I was a baby,

00:19:01.700 --> 00:19:04.870
and I was taken in by the Randalls.

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:12.260
Nevertheless, not a day goes by where
we here in Togetsu do not remember you.

00:19:13.260 --> 00:19:15.050
This is going nowhere.

00:19:15.050 --> 00:19:17.550
I came here to ask something.

00:19:17.550 --> 00:19:22.600
Do you have anything to do with
the Others research facility?

00:19:22.600 --> 00:19:26.650
Sister Kasane, we must reveal
the truth to you.

00:19:26.650 --> 00:19:31.650
However, we are your people,
and the truth is for your ears alone.

00:19:31.650 --> 00:19:36.610
Forgive us, but would you come inside
so we may speak in private?

00:19:39.030 --> 00:19:40.660
No.

00:19:40.660 --> 00:19:44.910
Whatever you say to me,
I'll end up telling my platoon.

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:49.000
So telling me here, right now,
is the exact same thing.

00:19:51.630 --> 00:19:57.630
Then regrettably, we have
no choice but to resort to force.

00:20:01.600 --> 00:20:03.810
What's their problem?

00:20:03.810 --> 00:20:06.480
I think they mean it.

00:20:08.190 --> 00:20:09.900
Huh?!

00:20:09.900 --> 00:20:11.520
Shiden!

00:20:14.280 --> 00:20:15.990
We're outnumbered.

00:20:15.990 --> 00:20:17.860
Let them go!

00:20:32.630 --> 00:20:34.380
Kyoka?!

00:20:34.380 --> 00:20:36.420
What's going on?!

00:20:37.720 --> 00:20:39.220
Kasane!

00:20:44.600 --> 00:20:50.020
We now have the brain
that governs the Red Strings.

00:20:50.020 --> 00:20:53.570
The other one is heading this way.

00:20:54.860 --> 00:20:58.190
Forgive me, Kasane.

00:21:06.580 --> 00:21:08.330
So this is Togetsu.

00:21:08.330 --> 00:21:11.920
It's just as forlorn as I imagined.

00:21:18.260 --> 00:21:20.130
He has arrived.

00:21:20.130 --> 00:21:22.890
Brother Yuito is here.

00:21:25.470 --> 00:21:26.930
We welcome you.

00:21:26.930 --> 00:21:30.600
Huh? Oh, um... Hello.

00:21:31.940 --> 00:21:34.770
Sister Hanabi Ichijo.

00:21:34.770 --> 00:21:37.900
We owe your uncle a great debt.

00:21:37.900 --> 00:21:42.280
Huh?! Oh, okay!
We appreciate all you've done.

00:21:42.280 --> 00:21:47.950
Thank you for coming to greet us,
even though we showed up without notice.

00:21:47.950 --> 00:21:51.080
Anyway, um... we--

00:21:51.080 --> 00:21:55.130
You are interested in our knowledge,
are you not?

00:21:55.130 --> 00:21:58.510
What? I mean, yes, but...

00:21:58.510 --> 00:22:01.930
You are our special guests.

00:22:01.930 --> 00:22:07.140
I believe you shall find
what you seek here.

00:22:11.020 --> 00:22:13.270
This way, if you please.

00:22:13.270 --> 00:22:17.480
The Moon is watching over you.

00:24:09.170 --> 00:24:11.970
THE MOON'S SECRETS
